# Tickets, comments and metrics. Run in order: later requests reuse tokens and ids from earlier ones.
# Seed users all have the password Password123!
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1

### 1. Log in: Ana (customer)
# @name ana
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ana@example.com", "password": "Password123!" }

### 2. Log in: Lucía (agent)
# @name lucia
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "lucia@triage.dev", "password": "Password123!" }

### 3. Log in: Carlos (another customer)
# @name carlos
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "carlos@example.com", "password": "Password123!" }

### 4. Log in: admin
# @name admin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@triage.dev", "password": "Password123!" }

### 5. Ana opens a ticket: 201 + Location header, status open, priority medium, no assignee
# @name created
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Export button does nothing", "description": "Clicking Export on the reports page has no effect." }

### 6. Ana lists tickets: only HER tickets come back
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}

### 7. Ana tries to set the priority: 403 (agents triage)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{created.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "priority": "urgent" }

### 8. Carlos asks for Ana's ticket: 404, not 403 (he must not learn it exists)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{created.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{carlos.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}

### 9. Lucía's queue: open + unassigned, most urgent first
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets?status=open&assigneeId=none&sort=-priority
Authorization: Bearer {{lucia.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}

### 10. Lucía searches by title, 5 per page
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets?q=export&page=1&limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{lucia.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}

### 11. Lucía triages: priority high
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{created.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{lucia.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "priority": "high" }

### 12. Skipping a step: open -> resolved is not allowed: 409 INVALID_STATUS_TRANSITION
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{lucia.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "resolved" }

### 13. Lucía starts work: in_progress, and she becomes the assignee automatically
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{lucia.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "in_progress" }

### 14. Lucía leaves an internal note (customers never see it)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{lucia.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Reproduced: the export endpoint returns 500 for this account.", "isInternal": true }

### 15. Lucía replies to Ana
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{lucia.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Thanks Ana, we found the cause and are working on a fix." }

### 16. Ana reads the conversation: only the public reply
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}

### 17. Lucía reads it: the reply AND the internal note
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{lucia.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}

### 18. Ana tries to write an internal note: 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Secret note", "isInternal": true }

### 19. Lucía resolves it: resolvedAt is set
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{lucia.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "resolved" }

### 20. Ana reopens it: back to open, resolvedAt cleared
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "open" }

### 21. Assigning a ticket to a customer: 422 INVALID_ASSIGNEE
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/assignee
Authorization: Bearer {{lucia.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "assigneeId": "{{carlos.response.body.$.user.id}}" }

### 22. Unassign: back to the queue
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/assignee
Authorization: Bearer {{lucia.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "assigneeId": null }

### 23. Invalid filters: 400 with one error per query parameter
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets?status=closed&limit=500&sort=newest
Authorization: Bearer {{lucia.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}

### 24. Admin: metrics for the last 30 days (default range)
GET {{baseUrl}}/metrics/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}

### 25. Admin: metrics for a custom range
GET {{baseUrl}}/metrics/summary?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}

### 26. Metrics with `from` after `to`: 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/metrics/summary?from=2026-10-31&to=2026-10-01
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}

### 27. An agent asks for metrics: 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/metrics/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{lucia.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}

### 28. Admin deletes the ticket (its comments go with it): 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{created.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}

### 29. It's gone: 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{created.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.tokens.accessToken}}
